      "content": "but \"judicial review\" and \"evidence-based\" measures usually take way too long when an attack is actually happening in real-time. if a country has to wait for a court to approve a shutdown while their infrastructure is being destroyed, they've already lost. don't you think that makes your \"strict limits\" more of a theoretical ideal than something that actually works in the real world of modern cyber warfare?",
